{"id": "a52e68d9-1230-44e9-8e42-f5bcb304f8b7", "transcript": [{"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Thanks for calling Finch Legal, this is Carlos. How can I help you today?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Hi Carlos. I'm calling because I slipped and fell at a grocery store a few months back—Safeway on Aurora Avenue North—and I'm trying to figure out if I even have a case."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "I'm sorry that happened. Let's start with your full legal name and the best number to reach you, and I'll take down what happened."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Sure. My name is Maria Elena Gonzalez. You can reach me at 206-555-3847, and my email is maria.gonzalez84@gmail.com."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Thank you, Maria. Walk me through the fall—what date was it, and what caused you to slip?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "It was May 26th last year—2024. I was walking down the aisle and my foot went straight into a puddle of spilled olive oil. Dios mío, I went down hard. There were no wet floor signs anywhere."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Did anyone see it happen, or were there employees nearby right after?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Two employees came over and helped me up pretty fast. They were nice about it, but they didn't start an incident report until I asked them to—I had to push a little, honestly."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Understood. What injuries did you notice right away, and where did you go for treatment?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "My lower back seized up and my right wrist was killing me. Later that day I went to the ER at Swedish Medical Center. X-rays didn't show any fractures, but they diagnosed a lumbar strain and a right wrist sprain. Dr. Amit Chandra was the attending who saw me through follow-up."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Have you done any therapy or other treatment since then?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Yeah—I've had eight sessions at Evergreen PT. It helped, but I'm not a hundred percent. I'm thirty-four, and I work for Amazon Flex here in Seattle—mostly loading my car and delivering packages to doorsteps—and anything with lifting boxes really aggravates the wrist."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "How much work did you miss because of this?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "About two full weeks off the app. That hurt—this is how I pay my bills, and I couldn't keep up the pace without making the pain worse."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Do you have a rough total on medical bills so far?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "I'm sitting at around forty-two hundred dollars—about $4,200—with what's been billed to date."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "I need to ask a few standard questions. Any prior injuries to your back or wrist, and any past legal claims or lawsuits?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "I had a minor wrist thing maybe five years ago—totally healed, nothing like this. And three years ago I picked up a misdemeanor DUI; I did what the court asked and it's resolved. No other injury cases."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Have you spoken with any other attorneys about this incident, or filed anything with Safeway's insurance yourself?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "No other lawyers—this is my first call. I haven't filed anything on my own yet; I didn't want to mess it up."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "That's smart. Do you carry your own health insurance, and do you know if MedPay or anything similar might apply on your auto policy—we sometimes see that with gig drivers?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "I have health insurance through the marketplace. I haven't dug into the car policy side—honestly I wasn't sure if that even mattered for a slip and fall inside a store."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Fair question—we can sort that out. Practically speaking, what documents do you already have—photos, the incident report, discharge papers?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "I have photos of the aisle and the oil, the incident report number, and my Swedish discharge packet. What else should I be gathering, and realistically how long does something like this take?"}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Grab your PT notes and billing statements from Evergreen, any work logs or earnings summaries from Amazon Flex for those two weeks, and receipts for out-of-pocket costs. Timelines vary, but premises cases often take months of treatment documentation before demand—I'll have our team review and give you a clearer map."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Okay—that's helpful. So next step is you guys review and call me back?"}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Exactly. I'm going to summarize: slip on spilled olive oil at Safeway Aurora on May 26, 2024, no wet floor signs, ER at Swedish with Dr. Chandra, eight visits at Evergreen PT, roughly $4,200 in bills, two weeks off Amazon Flex. We'll verify coverage, request any missing records, and schedule a follow-up with you at 206-555-3847 and maria.gonzalez84@gmail.com. Anything you want to add before we wrap?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "No—that covers it. Thanks, Carlos."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "You're welcome, Maria. We'll be in touch soon with next steps."}], "outcome_status": "settled", "outcome_value": 47500}
{"id": "d3f899da-d6f7-41e7-a8cb-6fb8b055b882", "transcript": [{"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Thank you for calling Finch Legal, this is Brenda. How can I help you today?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Hi Brenda, thanks for taking my call. My name is Priya Patel. I was in a car accident a few months ago and I have a bunch of questions—I actually have notes in front of me so I don't forget anything."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Of course, Priya. Take your time—that's exactly what we want. Walk me through what happened when you're ready."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Okay. On March fourteenth, twenty twenty-four, I was a passenger in an Uber on I-95 southbound, right around the Cypress Creek Road exit in Broward County. Traffic had slowed suddenly and a pickup truck rear-ended us—I think he was going maybe forty-five when he hit us."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "I'm sorry you went through that. Were you able to get information from the other driver and your Uber driver?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Yes. Our Uber driver's name was Demetrius Hall. The truck driver said his name was Craig—he gave me his insurance card. It was Progressive; I took a photo of the card but I honestly don't remember the policy number off the top of my head, it's in my notes."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "That's fine—we can work with the carrier name and what you have. Did law enforcement come to the scene?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "They did. Officer Daniels with the Broward County Sheriff's Office filed the report. The report number is 2024-BR-08831—I wrote that down twice because I was worried I'd transpose digits."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Good—that helps a lot. Were you injured, and did you go to the hospital?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "I went by ambulance to Broward Health Medical Center. Dr. Natasha Volkov evaluated me—she diagnosed a herniated disc at C5-C6, whiplash, and a left shoulder strain. I've been in physical therapy three times a week at Coastal Spine and Rehab for about two months now, and they say I'll probably need more."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "How has this affected your day-to-day and your work, if you don't mind sharing?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "I'm twenty-nine, I'm a software engineer at a fintech startup in Fort Lauderdale. I missed six weeks of work. My company was understanding about PTO, but I'm really stressed about the stock vesting timeline—I lost time I can't really get back, and I'm trying to understand if any of that is recoverable legally."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "That's a fair question, and it's something we can explore with the team. Do you have a sense of your medical expenses so far?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Roughly eighteen thousand dollars so far, and I expect more with ongoing PT. I have health insurance through work—Aetna—so some of it's been processed through them, but I kept copies of bills and EOBs in a folder."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Perfect. Since you were in an Uber, there can be multiple layers of coverage—the at-fault driver's insurance, and potentially Uber's commercial policy depending on the phase of the ride. Did you take any photos at the scene?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Yes, I took photos of both vehicles and the area. I wasn't sure how Uber's insurance interacts with Craig's Progressive policy—like who pays first—and that's one of the things I wanted to ask. I read a little online but the timelines confused me."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Totally understandable. Generally we map out available policies, put the other side on notice, and build your treatment story before we talk settlement. Typical timelines depend on how you heal and how responsive the carriers are, but I'll make sure an attorney walks you through what to expect step by step."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "How long does something like this usually take from intake to resolution? I'm—I talk fast when I'm nervous, sorry—I'm just trying to plan around performance reviews and whether I need to disclose anything to HR."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "No need to apologize. Many cases take months, sometimes longer if treatment continues or if we need litigation, but you won't be guessing in the dark—we'll give you milestones. As for HR, that's personal, but lots of clients keep it private unless they need accommodations."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Okay. I don't have any prior injuries I'm aware of, and I've never been involved in a lawsuit or anything like that. I want to make sure I'm not doing anything that accidentally hurts my case—should I keep posting on social media, talk to Progressive if they call?"}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Great questions. We'll send guidance on communications with insurers—usually you want to be careful about recorded statements early on. Limiting social posts about the accident is wise too."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Got it. My direct line is 954-555-2190, and my email is priya.patel.dev@gmail.com—those are the best ways to reach me. Is there anything else you need from me today?"}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Thank you, I've got those. If you can email us the Progressive card photo, the police report number you already gave, and any billing you've organized, that jump-starts our file. We'll also confirm the Uber trip details if you have the receipt in the app."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "I can do that tonight—everything's basically scanned already. One last thing: will someone actually call me back with a clear checklist, or is it all portal-based? I work better when I know the order of operations."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "You'll get a written checklist and a call from our team so you have both. We'll outline records requests, lien issues with Aetna if they apply, and how we coordinate with Progressive and any Uber-related coverage."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "That helps a lot. I feel a little less spun up already."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "I'm glad. To recap: March fourteenth rear-end on I-95 near Cypress Creek as an Uber passenger, report 2024-BR-08831, treatment with Dr. Volkov and Coastal Spine, about eighteen thousand in bills so far, work and vesting impact, photos and documentation ready. Next step is we complete intake, an attorney reviews within a few business days, and we schedule a follow-up to discuss strategy and timing."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Perfect. I'll send the email with attachments tonight. Thank you, Brenda."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "You're welcome, Priya. We'll be in touch soon—take care of yourself in the meantime."}], "outcome_status": "settled", "outcome_value": 127500}
{"id": "ed261d89-c76b-4ec8-8e7f-cb6a9f662b14", "transcript": [{"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Thank you for calling Finch Legal Intake, this is Alex. How can I help you today?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Hi Alex. My name is Marcus Deshawn Williams. I was in a car accident last summer and I have been trying to handle the insurance piece on my own, but it is getting messy. I read a few articles about how pre-existing stuff gets argued and I figured I should talk to someone who actually does this every day."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "I am glad you reached out, Marcus. I will walk through the facts with you so we can see how we might help. Can you start with when and where the collision happened?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "June 21st, 2023. I was heading through the intersection of Commonwealth Avenue and Massachusetts Avenue in Boston. I had a solid green and I was in my 2019 Honda Civic. Out of nowhere a Mercedes SUV came through on the red and T-boned me on the driver side."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "That sounds frightening. Do you know who the other driver was, and whether there was any indication of distraction or negligence?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Her name is Katherine Holloway. A witness, an older couple, told the officer she was on her phone. I did not see the phone myself, I was too busy getting spun, but Frank and Doris Abernathy both gave statements to the police. Their names are probably in the report."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "That is helpful. Did Boston Police respond, and do you have a report number?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Yes. Officer Ramirez took the report. The number is 23-BOS-44219. I have a copy somewhere in my email if you need it later."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Perfect. Were you taken to the hospital from the scene?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Embarrassing in hindsight, but no. I felt shaken and sore and I told myself I was fine. Classic mistake, I guess. About a week later I could not turn my neck without pain shooting down my arm. That is when I knew this was not just stiffness."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Delayed treatment is common after adrenaline wears off. Insurers sometimes try to use gaps in care against claimants, so we will want a clear timeline from the crash through your first visit. Where did you go first?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Mass General. I saw Dr. James Fitzgerald. He diagnosed cervical radiculopathy, muscle strain, and said the wreck aggravated degenerative disc disease I already had at L4-L5. I am forty-one, freelance graphic designer, so I spend a lot of time at a desk. Sitting for long stretches has been brutal."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Thank you for being upfront about the pre-existing condition. That is not a disqualifier, but carriers love to argue everything was old. We counter that with aggravation theory and treating records. Have you had similar issues documented before?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Yeah, and I want to be straight about it. About four years ago I had another car accident with a back injury. That case settled for fifteen thousand dollars through the other insurer. I know the defense will wave that around like a flag. It is frustrating because this feels worse, but I get why they will try."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Prior claims are part of the picture, not the whole story. What treatment are you doing now for this crash?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Physical therapy at Boston Sports Medicine, plus a couple of epidural injections when the nerve pain flared. Bills are around twelve thousand five hundred and still climbing with follow-ups."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "How has work been affected? You mentioned freelancing."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "I probably lost close to three weeks of real billable time, and a few clients drifted because I could not hit deadlines while I was piecing myself together. Not dramatic enough for reality TV, but it hits the wallet."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Understood. Which insurance companies are involved on your side and theirs?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Her policy is Geico. I carry my own auto insurance through Liberty Mutual. I have not given a recorded statement to Geico yet because everything I read said to be careful with that."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Good instinct on recorded statements. Any criminal history we should be aware of? Sometimes carriers run background checks."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "None. Clean record. My rap sheet is mostly bad font choices on client decks, if that counts."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Noted, no priors. Best way to reach you if an attorney reviews this file?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Phone is 617-555-8103. Email is marcus.w.designs@outlook.com. Text is fine if I am in a session with a client."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Thank you. One more thing on timing: from the week you waited before Mass General, did Dr. Fitzgerald link the symptoms clearly to the collision in his notes?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "He did. He wrote that the mechanism fit the new radicular symptoms and that the prior degeneration was asymptomatic until the impact. Reading that line felt like a small win after I had been spiraling about the old case."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "That documentation helps push back on a pure pre-existing defense. Is there anything else you want us to know about witnesses or property damage?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "The Civic took the worst of it on the driver door and B-pillar area. The Abernathys stuck around until police finished. I am hoping their statements about the phone and the red light carry weight."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Here is a quick recap: red-light T-bone at Commonwealth and Mass Ave on June 21, 2023, report 23-BOS-44219, Katherine Holloway as other driver, Geico on her side, Liberty Mutual for you, treatment at Mass General with Dr. Fitzgerald including PT at Boston Sports Medicine and injections, roughly twelve thousand five hundred in bills so far, prior back claim from four years ago settled for fifteen thousand, and strong witness support from Frank and Doris Abernathy."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "That is accurate. The only footnote is my pride, which is still recovering from admitting I waited a week."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "We will frame that delay clinically, not as negligence on your part. Next steps: I am forwarding this intake to our litigation team for a conflict check and case assessment. You should hear within two business days about scheduling a deeper consult. Please do not speak with Geico beyond basic facts until then, and gather any photos, repair estimates, and wage records you have."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "I appreciate the clarity, Alex. I will round up the paperwork and wait for your call."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "You are welcome, Marcus. We will be in touch at 617-555-8103 or marcus.w.designs@outlook.com. Take care."}], "outcome_status": "trial", "outcome_value": 285000}
{"id": "892cde08-34cb-4d9f-b64d-679827a9a65a", "transcript": [{"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Thank you for calling Finch Legal Intake, this is Diana. How can I help you today?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Yeah, hi. My name is Robert Chen—everybody calls me Bobby. I need to talk to somebody about a bad wreck I was in with a semi truck."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "I'm sorry you went through that, Bobby. I'm going to ask you some questions so we can understand what happened. Can I get a good callback number and an email for you?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Sure. Phone is 520-555-6214. Email is bobbychen1972 at yahoo dot com—bobbychen1972@yahoo.com."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Got it, thank you. Walk me through the accident—when and where did this happen?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "April eighth, twenty twenty-four. I was eastbound on I-10 outside Tucson, right around mile marker 248. We had one of those dust storms roll through—you could barely see."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "That sounds frightening. What happened with the truck?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "It was a Sysco food services eighteen-wheeler. Thing jackknifed right in front of me. I slammed the brakes but there was no chance. I rear-ended the trailer in my Ford F-150. Truck's totaled."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Were you able to get out on your own, or did emergency services have to extricate you?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "They flew me out. Helicopter. I still get shaky talking about it—my kids heard I was airlifted before they knew I was alive. That messed me up almost as much as the wreck."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "I'm really glad you're here to tell us about it. Where did they take you?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Banner University Medical Center. I don't remember much of the first day, but I was there five days total."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "What injuries did the doctors diagnose?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Three broken ribs on my left side, punctured my right lung—pneumothorax, they kept saying. Grade two concussion, mild TBI. And I split my forehead open bad—fourteen stitches. Surgeon on my case was Dr. Patricia Morales."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "That's a significant trauma. Are you still under care?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Yeah. I'm doing physical therapy and occupational therapy at Tucson Rehabilitation Associates. I also see a neurologist, Dr. Kevin Obasi, for the post-concussion stuff—headaches, my memory's shot sometimes, hard to focus."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Linda says to tell you she's got a folder with all the appointment dates if you need them—my wife Linda, she's been running point on all this."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Please thank Linda for us—we'll want those records. Bobby, have you been able to work since the accident?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "No. And that's... that's the hardest part, honestly. I'm fifty-two. I'm a construction foreman for Kiewit Construction. My whole life I'm the guy who climbs, lifts, runs equipment. Now I can't do any of it. Company put me on disability but it ain't the same. My identity's my job."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "It makes sense that hits you hard. We'll want to document how this changed your day-to-day and your earnings."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Medical bills are already over eighty-seven thousand dollars. I got workers' comp through Kiewit, and my auto insurance is State Farm. I don't know how all that plays together—I just know the mailbox is full of bills."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Workers' comp can interact with a third-party claim in specific ways; our team will sort through coordination of benefits. Was there any citation or fault finding related to the truck driver?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Troopers cited him for excessive speed for conditions. Dust storm, low visibility, and he was still moving too fast for what was happening."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Thank you. Any prior similar injuries or claims we should know about?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Nope. Never been hurt like this. Clean driving record too—I've been driving rigs and pickups on job sites twenty-five years without something like this."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Is there anyone else at home helping you besides Linda with appointments and recovery?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Mostly Linda. She's tough as nails but I see the toll—she's managing my meds, driving me to PT, dealing with the kids' worry. I hate being the guy on the couch."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Sorry—Linda's waving at me—she wants me to say we have photos of the scene and the Sysco trailer number from the police report."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "That's excellent. We'll want the police report, photos, and any workers' comp correspondence. Full legal name again for the file—Robert Chen, correct?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Full legal name is Robert Chen. Bobby's just my nickname—what everybody's called me my whole life."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Understood. Let me summarize: semi jackknife on I-10 near mile 248 during a dust storm, helicopter to Banner, serious thoracic and head injuries with ongoing neuro and rehab, work loss as a foreman, workers' comp and State Farm in the mix, driver cited for speed for conditions."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "That's the long and short of it. I just want straight answers and somebody who'll go toe-to-toe with a big company if it comes to that."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Next steps: I'm assigning this to our serious injury team. They'll verify coverage, order records from Banner and your therapists, and reach out within two business days. If anything gets worse medically, go to the ER and keep us posted."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Okay. Five-two-zero five-five-five six-two-one-four and bobbychen1972@yahoo.com if anything drops."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "We have both. Take care of yourself, Bobby, and give Linda our thanks. We're glad you called."}], "outcome_status": "settled", "outcome_value": 465000}
{"id": "63b564e4-ab4a-469b-88b4-72492f8e09fe", "transcript": [{"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Thank you for calling Finch Legal Intake, this is Carlos. How can I help you today?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Hi Carlos. My name is Sandra Reeves. I'm calling about my daughter. I— I don't even know where to start. Something terrible happened to her."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Sandra, I'm really sorry you're going through this. Take your time. I'm here to listen, and we'll go at whatever pace feels okay for you."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Thank you. It's Lily—Lily Reeves. She's eight. On September first, 2024, she was just playing in our front yard on Elm Street, here in Highlands Ranch in Denver. Our neighbor's dog got through the fence and attacked her."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "I'm so sorry. Can you tell me your full address on Elm, and who owns the dog?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "We live at 4222 Elm Street. The dog's owner is Gregory Polk at 4218 Elm. It's a Rottweiler named Tank. I've told Greg twice that dog was aggressive through that fence. Twice. And six months ago it lunged at our mail carrier—I know that because the carrier told me."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "That helps a lot, Sandra. Walk me through exactly how Tank got to Lily that day."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "There was a gap in the fence—I've been worried about it. Tank pushed through and was on her before I could get there. I pulled him off. I called nine-one-one. Denver Police came, paramedics—she went by ambulance to Children's Hospital Colorado."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "You did everything you could in an impossible moment. What injuries did the doctors document for Lily?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Deep cuts on her right cheek and jaw—they needed twenty-seven stitches. Her right ear was torn; Dr. Amanda Chen, she's a pediatric plastic surgeon, did reconstructive surgery. She has puncture wounds on her right arm too. The bills are already about forty-three thousand dollars."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Has the care team said anything about surgeries Lily may need as she grows?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Yes. They said at least two more reconstructive surgeries over the next three years, maybe more, because her face will change as she grows. I'm trying not to fall apart when I think about her looking in the mirror for the rest of her life."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "How has Lily been doing emotionally since she came home?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "She has severe nightmares. She won't go outside. She's seeing Dr. Miriam Katz, a child psychologist, twice a week. My voice keeps cracking—I teach middle school, I'm supposed to be strong for kids, and I can't fix this for my own child."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "What you're describing—pain, fear, therapy—that's real harm, not just physical. Has animal control been involved with Tank?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "They seized the dog. It's in quarantine now. Part of me is furious at Greg, part of me is just terrified this could happen to another child if we don't do something."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "I hear you wanting accountability and prevention. On insurance—who is covering Lily's treatment so far, and do you know if Mr. Polk has homeowner's coverage?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "My insurance is through Kaiser Permanente from my job. Greg's homeowner's is Allstate—that's what another neighbor mentioned when all of this blew up. I want to make sure we're not the only ones paying for what his dog did."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Understood. For our file, what's your household situation, and have you spoken with any other lawyers about this?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "I'm a middle school teacher. My husband Derek Reeves is a firefighter. We have not talked to any attorney before this call— you're the first."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Since Lily is a minor, parents usually bring claims on her behalf. Settlements for children often require court approval to protect the child's long-term interests, and funds can be structured so they help her into adulthood. Does that address what you were asking about her rights?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Yes— I need to know she has long-term rights, not just a check that disappears. I want this documented so it never happens again to her or anyone else on this block."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "The prior complaints and the mail carrier incident matter for showing this wasn't a one-off. We'll want dates if you have them, photos of the fence, and any animal control or police reports. How can we reach you, Sandra?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "My phone is 303-555-7821. Email is sandra.reeves.teacher@gmail.com. Lily's last name is Reeves, same as mine—Lily Reeves, eight years old."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Thank you. One more thing on damages—we'll look at medical costs past and future, the psychological care with Dr. Katz, scarring and disfigurement, and how this changed Lily's daily life. Does that match what you're experiencing as a family?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "It does. She's not the same little girl who used to ride her bike on the sidewalk. I'm angry at Greg for ignoring me, and I'm scared every time the door opens."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "That anger and fear make sense. We'll treat this with the seriousness it deserves. Is there anything else you think we should know about Tank, the fence, or witnesses?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Neighbors saw the ambulance. The mail carrier might remember the earlier incident if someone reaches out. I have photos of the gap in the fence I texted my husband the week before—I should have forced the issue harder with Greg."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "You raised concerns; that's not on you. We'll want those photos and any texts. Sandra, you've given me a clear picture: severe dog bite to Lily Reeves on September 1, 2024, at 4222 Elm Street, Denver, dog and owner Gregory Polk at 4218 Elm, history of aggression and prior warnings, care at Children's Hospital Colorado with Dr. Amanda Chen, ongoing psychology with Dr. Miriam Katz, animal control seizure and quarantine of Tank, Kaiser and Allstate in play, and significant future surgical needs."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "That's— yes. That's all of it. What happens now?"}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Next steps: an attorney on our team will review this intake today, order police and animal control records, and likely send preservation letters regarding the fence and the dog. We'll call you at 303-555-7821 to schedule a deeper consult, and we'll explain how we protect Lily's interests as a minor every step of the way."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Okay. I just want her safe and I want someone to take this seriously. Thank you for not rushing me."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Always. You're doing right by Lily. We'll be in touch soon, Sandra—and again, I'm truly sorry your family is carrying this."}], "outcome_status": "trial", "outcome_value": 3200000}
{"id": "cac3df82-f1fa-4dfa-bbfe-4d4c18cf0a59", "transcript": [{"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Thank you for calling. This is Alex. I handle workplace injury intakes. How can I help you today?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Hi Alex. My name is Darnell Marcus Washington. I am thirty-six. I am a journeyman electrician with Pinnacle Electrical Contractors here in Atlanta, and I need to talk to someone about a serious fall I took on a job site."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "I am sorry you are going through this, Darnell. Walk me through what happened, including the date and location if you have them."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "February twelfth, twenty twenty-four. I was at Peachtree Crossing Apartments, new construction off Peachtree Industrial Boulevard. I was up on scaffolding doing rough-in when the whole thing gave way. I dropped about fifteen feet."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "That is a significant fall. Who controlled the site, and do you know anything about how the scaffolding was set up?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Turner-Mitchell Construction is the general contractor. The scaffolding was not right. Cross braces were missing, and the base plates were sitting on ground that was not stable. I have been keeping notes because I knew this was sloppy the second I stepped on it."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Have OSHA or any safety authority been involved, and were there witnesses on site?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "My co-workers Jamal Brooks and Eric Sandoval, both electricians on our crew, saw the whole thing. Site foreman Mike Petersen called nine-one-one. I am furious because OSHA already cited Turner-Mitchell for scaffolding violations at a different site six months before my fall."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "That prior citation pattern can matter for how we look at negligence against the general contractor. Where were you taken for emergency care?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Ambulance to Grady Memorial Hospital. I broke my left femur, tore the ACL in my left knee, and fractured three vertebrae. Dr. Raymond Okafor, orthopedics, did femur rodding and ACL reconstruction. I was inpatient eight days."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "What is your recovery looking like now, and are you getting rehabilitation?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "I am in a wheelchair and working toward crutches. Physical therapy three times a week at Shepherd Center. I am the sole breadwinner for my wife Keisha and our three kids, four, seven, and eleven years old, and I am scared about how long this is going to take."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Workers compensation is usually the first layer on a construction injury. What carrier is involved, and how are they treating the claim?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Pinnacle carries workers comp through Hartford Insurance. They have paid some bills, but they are denying the knee surgery as not work-related, which is insulting. I tore that ACL when I hit the ground from their unsafe scaffolding. I get heated just saying it out loud."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Do you already have counsel on the comp side, and are you looking at a separate path against the general contractor or other third parties?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "I have Lisa Trammel at Trammel and Associates handling workers comp. I still want a personal injury firm to go after Turner-Mitchell directly. The GC controls site safety and coordinates subs like us. If their scaffolding program was a mess, that is on them, not just on my employer."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "That distinction matters. We often see third-party claims where the general contractor owes independent duties on a multi-employer work site, separate from what your employer owes you under comp."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "That is what I have been reading. Pinnacle did not build that scaffold. Turner-Mitchell’s people were running the site. My union rep from IBEW Local six thirteen told me to call and get PI counsel involved before evidence walks off the lot."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Smart advice from the union. What kind of medical expenses are we talking about so far?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "About one hundred twenty-four thousand dollars in medical bills and counting. I am organized—I keep a binder—but I am not used to asking for help. I am practical: I need someone who knows how to pressure a GC with OSHA history and real damages."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "I want your best contact information and permission to note your family situation for urgency and lost wage analysis."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Phone 404-555-9382. Email dwashington.ibew@gmail.com. Again, Darnell Marcus Washington. Keisha and the kids are depending on me to get this right."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Understood. I have Peachtree Crossing, Turner-Mitchell as GC, Hartford on comp with a knee surgery denial, Grady and Dr. Okafor, witnesses Jamal Brooks and Eric Sandoval, foreman Mike Petersen, prior OSHA scaffolding citation within six months at another site, and Lisa Trammel on comp."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "That is everything I have documented. If you need photos from Jamal or statements, I can coordinate. I just do not want Turner-Mitchell pretending this was a freak accident when their own pattern says otherwise."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Next steps: our team will run a conflict check, pull the OSHA file if available, and have an attorney call you within one business day. We will coordinate with Ms. Trammel so comp strategy and third-party strategy do not step on each other."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "I appreciate that. Comp is one fight; Turner-Mitchell is another. I need both handled clean."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "We will also flag preservation letters for scaffold materials, inspection logs, and subcontractor communications. Do not sign anything from Hartford or Turner-Mitchell without us reviewing it."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "I will not. I have been burned enough by that knee denial."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "You did the right thing calling. Watch for our callback at the number you gave, and email us anything new from PT or Shepherd Center as it comes in."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Thank you, Alex. I will send what I have tonight. I need my family protected and I need accountability on that site."}], "outcome_status": "settled", "outcome_value": 185000}
{"id": "ecb99c86-138b-4b5c-a25f-fb26be6b6e79", "transcript": [{"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Thank you for calling Finch. This is Carlos. May I have your name and a brief reason for your call?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Hi. Um, this is Tyler Nakamura. I'm calling about—I got hurt by a blender. My mom is here with me."}, {"speaker": "[Keiko Nakamura, in background]", "text": "Hello, I'm Keiko Nakamura, Tyler's mother. I'm on speaker. We need to understand what options Tyler has."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Hi Tyler, hi Keiko. I'll ask you both questions—Tyler, I'll want your words on what happened, and Keiko, please jump in on dates and medical details. Sound okay?"}, {"speaker": "[Keiko Nakamura, in background]", "text": "Yes. On June fifteenth, twenty twenty-three, at our home in Scottsdale, Arizona, Tyler was using our kitchen blender."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "I was just making a smoothie after school. Like, normal stuff."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Do you recall the brand, model, and where it was purchased?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "It's a Ninja Professional Blender. The model number on the box says BL660. We got it at Target on Scottsdale Road—maybe three months before, something like that."}, {"speaker": "[Keiko Nakamura, in background]", "text": "I have the receipt. I keep major purchases organized."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Walk me through the moment it failed."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "While it was running, the blade assembly—I don't know the word—detached? And the glass pitcher basically shattered. It happened really fast."}, {"speaker": "[Keiko Nakamura, in background]", "text": "I drove him immediately to HonorHealth Scottsdale Osborn Emergency Department."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "What injuries did Tyler suffer?"}, {"speaker": "[Keiko Nakamura, in background]", "text": "A deep laceration across his right palm and two severed tendons in his index and middle fingers."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Who performed the repair and what follow-up care did he have?"}, {"speaker": "[Keiko Nakamura, in background]", "text": "Emergency surgery by Dr. Lisa Yamamoto, a hand surgeon. He was in a cast for six weeks, then a splint for four additional weeks."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Yeah, that part sucked. Couldn't really use my hand at all for a while."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Is he in therapy now?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "I'm going to hand therapy at Arizona Hand and Wrist Specialists. Twice a week."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "How would Dr. Yamamoto describe his recovery?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "She said I've got back maybe seventy percent grip strength, but I might never get, like, full fine motor control in those fingers. Which is… yeah."}, {"speaker": "[Keiko Nakamura, in background]", "text": "He plays guitar—he's in the school jazz band—and he was hoping for a music scholarship. I'm upset this may be permanent. I've also seen other online complaints about this model and I'm reviewing recalls."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Have you contacted Ninja's customer service?"}, {"speaker": "[Keiko Nakamura, in background]", "text": "Yes. They emailed a prepaid label to return the blender for investigation and offered a two-hundred-dollar store credit. I declined. That is not proportionate to his harm."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Tyler, was anything photographed?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "My mom took pictures of the broken blender and my injury before we left for the ER. So, yeah, there's photos."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Medical expenses and insurance—what should we know?"}, {"speaker": "[Keiko Nakamura, in background]", "text": "Medical bills are approximately thirty-four thousand dollars to date. We are insured through my employer's plan, Blue Cross Blue Shield."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Any prior similar injuries or active legal matters for either of you?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "No. I haven't had anything like this before. No lawsuits or whatever."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Tyler, you're seventeen. For minors, a parent or guardian typically brings the claim, and any settlement usually requires court approval to protect your interests. Keiko, you'd be closely involved in authorizations and decisions."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Best phone numbers and an email for follow-up documents?"}, {"speaker": "[Keiko Nakamura, in background]", "text": "Tyler's cell is 480-555-1738. Mine is 480-555-1739. Email is keiko.nakamura@gmail.com."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Summary: we're looking at a product liability matter involving a Ninja BL660 purchased at Target, a blade assembly failure and shattered pitcher on June 15, 2023, serious hand injuries treated at HonorHealth with surgery by Dr. Yamamoto, ongoing therapy at Arizona Hand and Wrist Specialists, possible permanent fine motor limitations affecting music goals, manufacturer response limited to a return label and two-hundred-dollar credit, and photographic evidence preserved. Next steps: I'll send a retainer and intake packet to Keiko's email, and our team will request records from the hospital, surgeon, therapist, and insurer. If you think of anything else, reply to that email. Tyler, Keiko—thank you for the thorough information today."}], "outcome_status": "settled", "outcome_value": 82000}
{"id": "da9e2eaf-c7e0-4062-b81b-5b5127419fc8", "transcript": [{"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Thank you for calling Finch Legal Intake, this is Brenda. How may I help you today?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Yeah, hi. My name is Jesse Antonio Martinez. I need to talk to somebody about a motorcycle collision I was in—August third, twenty twenty-four. I have the sequence documented; I just want it handled correctly."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "I appreciate you reaching out, Jesse. I am going to take this step by step so we do not miss anything. Can I start with the best number to reach you and an email?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Phone is five-six-two, five-five-five, four-zero-nine-seven. Email is jesse dot martinez dot elec at gmail dot com."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Got it, thank you. Walk me through what happened, in your own words, from the moment before impact."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Roger. I was northbound on Pacific Coast Highway in Long Beach, approaching the intersection with Second Street. I was in my lane, steady speed, no lane splitting. White Chevy Tahoe, elderly driver, merged left without signaling—no blinker—and sideswiped me. Contact was driver-side of his vehicle to my right side. I went down and slid roughly thirty feet."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "That is very clear. Did law enforcement respond, and do you have a report number?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Long Beach PD. Officer Kim took the report. Report number is two-four dash LB dash five-five-one-nine-zero. I was not cited. Clean driving record, no priors on my end."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Were there any witnesses?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Yes. Rachel Torres was directly behind me in traffic. She stayed on scene. Her vehicle had a dashcam—front-facing—and it captured the entire lane change and the impact. I am stressing that because there is always motorcycle bias; people assume the rider was weaving or speeding. The video shows I did nothing wrong."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "I hear you on that bias, and we take it seriously when we build a file. The footage from Ms. Torres could be pivotal. Do you know the other driver’s name?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Harold Whitman, seventy-four. His auto carrier is AAA. My motorcycle policy is GEICO. Health coverage is through my union—IBEW."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Thank you. Were you transported for treatment?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Ambulance to Long Beach Memorial Medical Center. I was wearing full kit—DOT helmet, armored jacket, gloves, riding boots. That gear is probably why I am on this call instead of a worse outcome."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "I am glad you had that protection. What injuries were diagnosed?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Right clavicle fracture, torn rotator cuff on the right shoulder, road rash on the right hip and thigh that required skin grafts, and a fractured right wrist. Dr. Daniel Vasquez did the clavicle and rotator cuff—surgery August fifth. Dr. Michelle Park handled the graft work."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Understood. Any estimate on medical expenses to date?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "About sixty-seven thousand dollars billed so far, and I am not done with follow-up. The bike is totaled—twenty twenty-one Kawasaki Ninja six-fifty—insurance valued it around eighty-five hundred."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "What do you do for work, and how has this affected your income?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Licensed electrician with Pacific Power Solutions in Long Beach. I have been off work two months and counting. You cannot terminate conductors, pull wire, or work a ladder one-handed and stay compliant. The union has been supportive, but I need my shoulder and wrist back before I am useful on a job site."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Former military background—I noticed the way you structured the narrative. Does that influence how you have been documenting this?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Marines. Old habit: time, place, distance, sequence of events. I have been precise on PCH, Second Street, thirty feet of slide, no signal from Whitman, witness name Torres, dashcam confirmed. I do not want any of it diluted into “biker at fault” shorthand."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "We will preserve those facts and the witness information. How long have you been riding?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Twelve years. No prior injury claims. This one was on him—unsignaled lane change—and I need that reflected with the video, the police report, and the clinical record."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "I have Harold Whitman, AAA, Officer Kim, report twenty-four-LB-five-five-one-nine-zero, Rachel Torres and dashcam footage, GEICO on the motorcycle policy, IBEW health, Memorial, Dr. Vasquez and Dr. Park, union electrician with a significant lost-time component. Anything else you want in the file today?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Negative. That is the complete picture. If counsel needs the dashcam chain of custody or my gear list, I can produce it. I want forward motion on this."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Here is what happens next: I am opening your matter with your contact information, the August third PCH incident details, providers and carriers, and your work restrictions. A case team will review the police report and witness materials, then reach out to schedule a deeper intake and records collection."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Copy. I will watch for your call and email. Appreciate you not dismissing the motorcycle piece—means more than you might think."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "You are welcome, Jesse. We will be in touch shortly with those next steps. Take care."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Thank you, Brenda. Standing by."}], "outcome_status": "settled", "outcome_value": 225000}
{"id": "68808138-faf4-4e73-9d3a-fc8a770229ba", "transcript": [{"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Thank you for calling Finch Legal. This is Diana. How can I help you today?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Hi Diana. My name is Angela Denise Foster. I was hit by a car in a crosswalk in May and I need to understand what a case like mine usually looks like, compensation-wise, because I am bleeding money as a single mom."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "I am sorry you are going through that, Angela. I will take some details and then we can talk about how these matters generally work. When and where did the collision happen?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "May 16, 2024. I was on my lunch break from Banner Desert in Mesa—walking to Chipotle—and I crossed 7th Avenue at McDowell in Phoenix. I had the walk signal. A guy in a red Toyota Corolla rolled right on red straight into me while he was staring at his phone for GPS."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Did law enforcement respond, and was there any independent footage?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Yes. Phoenix PD. Officer Tran took the report—number 24-PHX-91047. There is security video from the Chase Bank on the corner; it caught the whole thing. The driver was a twenty-two-year-old named Ethan Birch. He was actually apologetic and stayed at the scene."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Thank you. Can you walk me through your injuries and treatment in your own words?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "I am an RN at Banner Desert, so I usually chart this stuff, not live it. I went over the hood, landed hard—compound fracture of the left tibia and fibula, deep contusion to the hip, and a grade two concussion. Paramedics transported me to St. Joseph's. The irony is not lost on me: charge nurse one week, patient with a neuro check and ortho consult the next."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "That sounds incredibly disruptive. What procedures or follow-up care have you had?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Open reduction internal fixation—titanium intramedullary rod and plates—by Dr. Carlos Medina, orthopedics. I was inpatient four days. Now I am partial weight-bearing with a walker, working toward a cane. I do PT three times a week at Select Physical Therapy."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "How has this affected your ability to work and your household?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "I have been off about three months. Twelve-hour shifts on my feet are not happening. Banner has held my job, but I am burning PTO and short-term disability fast. I have two teenagers—fourteen and sixteen—and I am the only income. My phone is 602-555-8214 and my email is angela.foster.rn@yahoo.com if you need them on file."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Got it. Do you have a rough sense of medical expenses to date, and how is coverage structured between health and auto?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Bills are around seventy-eight thousand. Health insurance is through Banner as my employer. The at-fault coverage is auto—Ethan Birch is on his parents' Farmers policy. No prior similar injuries, no legal baggage. I just need to know what people in pedestrian cases with surgical hardware and prolonged LOA typically see, ballpark."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "I hear you. Outcomes depend on liability clarity, policy limits, wage loss documentation, and how permanent the impairment is, but ORIF with rod and plates plus documented cognitive symptoms from a grade two concussion is serious. The bank camera and a favorable police report are strong facts."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Right—the open fracture with exposed bone is not something you soft-pedal on a pain scale. I am also watching for post-concussion symptoms; I know the return-to-work criteria for my unit better than I wish I did right now."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Are you still treating with neurology or primary care for the concussion, or mainly ortho and PT?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "PCP follow-up for neuro checks, ortho for the leg, PT for gait and strength. I am compliant—because again, I am the person who usually nags other people to complete their therapy."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Understood. Any lost benefits beyond PTO—401k match, shift differentials—that we should note?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Mostly base pay and differentials I am not picking up. The kids' schedules do not stop because Mom has a walker, so there is indirect cost too—rides, groceries delivered when I could not drive at first."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "We will capture those categories. Have you spoken with Farmers or given a recorded statement?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "I gave basic facts to their adjuster, no recorded statement. I was careful—I know how those get parsed."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Good. Anything else you want the attorney team to know about liability or your recovery trajectory?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Just that I was legally in the crosswalk with the signal, the driver admitted distraction, and the footage should make fault boringly obvious. Clinically I am hoping for union by radiograph, but I am realistic about arthritis risk long term."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Thank you, Angela. Here is a concise recap: pedestrian strike at 7th and McDowell on May 16, 2024, walk signal in your favor, Ethan Birch on parents' Farmers policy, report 24-PHX-91047, Chase camera, ORIF by Dr. Medina at St. Joseph's, PT at Select, ~$78k in bills, Banner health plan, three months off work, two minors at home."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "That is accurate. So what happens next—does someone call me about demand strategy and whether we are talking policy limits?"}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Next steps: I am sending this intake to our personal injury group today. A case manager will verify records and coverage, then an attorney will contact you within one business day to discuss valuation range, liens, and whether we open with a structured demand to Farmers."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Perfect. I appreciate you not talking to me like I have never seen an injury before—this has been surreal enough without the kindergarten explanations."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Of course. We will match your pace. If anything changes clinically or you get new imaging, email angela.foster.rn@yahoo.com updates to the same thread once we open your file. Take care of that leg."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Will do. Thanks, Diana."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "You are welcome. Goodbye for now."}], "outcome_status": "settled", "outcome_value": 345000}
{"id": "41b5e932-2d17-4ac6-943f-c10eb281270e", "transcript": [{"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Thank you for calling Finch Legal Intake, this is Diana. How can I help you today?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Hi. Um, my name is David Hyun Park. A friend basically told me I should call a lawyer after a car thing, and I honestly don't know if I even have... anything. It feels a little silly."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Hi David, not silly at all. People call for all kinds of reasons. Can you walk me through what happened, in your own words?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Sure. November fifteenth, twenty twenty-three, I was stopped at a red light on Boylston Street near the Prudential Center in Boston. A Toyota Camry bumped me from behind—really light, like maybe five miles an hour."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Okay. At the scene, were you hurt, and have you seen a doctor since then?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Not really hurt, and no doctor. We both got out. The other driver was a woman named Patricia Brennan. We exchanged info—her insurance is State Farm. It felt so minor we didn't call the police; we just handled it between us."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "I appreciate the detail. Any witnesses besides the two of you?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "No, just us."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "What kind of damage did your car have, and did you get it repaired?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Minor scuff and a small dent on the rear bumper. I paid eight hundred fifty dollars out of pocket to fix it. I still have the receipt."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Got it. After the accident, did you miss work or have any symptoms that lasted more than a day or two?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "I didn't miss any work—I'm IT support at Boston University. The next morning I felt a little stiff, but it went away fast. I never went in for it. My friend kept saying lawyers can get you something for pain and suffering, and I felt kind of sheepish because I'm not... I'm not really in pain."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "That makes sense, and thanks for being honest—that actually helps me give you a straight answer. Any prior injuries to your neck or back, or other accidents we should know about?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "No prior injuries, no legal history. This is the first time I've ever called a firm."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Okay. Can I get a good callback number and email for our file?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Yeah. Phone is six-one-seven, five-five-five, four-four-two-nine. Email is david.park.bu@gmail.com—D-A-V-I-D dot P-A-R-K dot B-U at Gmail."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Thank you, David Hyun Park, 617-555-4429, david.park.bu@gmail.com. Here's the gentle truth: most personal injury cases that move forward have documented treatment—someone examined you, there's a record, sometimes imaging or therapy. Without that, pain and suffering is very hard to prove, even when the accident definitely happened."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Yeah... I figured it might be weak. I didn't want to exaggerate anything. I just didn't want to leave money on the table if I was supposed to do something."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "You're not wrong to ask—that's smart. What you do have is a clear property-damage claim: you paid eight hundred fifty dollars and you have a receipt. That's separate from injury damages, and you can pursue that directly with State Farm as a third-party property claim."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "So for the injury side, you're saying there's not much there?"}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Based on what you've told me, an injury case wouldn't be something we'd take on—there isn't the medical documentation firms usually need to advocate effectively. That doesn't mean nothing happened; it just means the piece we handle isn't a fit here."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Okay. That's... actually a relief in a weird way. I didn't want to feel like I was faking anything."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "You weren't—and I'm glad you called. If you hit any snags with the property claim, you can also check in with your own auto insurer about guidance, but start with State Farm and your receipt. Is there anything else you want to ask before we wrap?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "No, that's really clear. Thank you for not making me feel dumb about it."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "You're welcome, David. Take care, and good luck getting that bumper expense sorted."}], "outcome_status": "dropped", "outcome_value": 0}
{"id": "30b0bdb6-ba20-4099-afcd-6064022237c2", "transcript": [{"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Thank you for calling Morgan & Associates, this is Brenda. How can I help you today?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Oh, hi Brenda—thank you for picking up. My name is Carmen Lucia Delgado, I'm fifty-one, and I'm calling because I slipped on black ice in my apartment parking lot back in January and I'm at my wit's end with Greystar and Aspen Ridge. I already tried one lawyer and he just… disappeared on me, so I'm hoping you all actually follow through."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "I'm so sorry you've been through that, Carmen. I want to make sure we capture everything correctly. Can you walk me through what happened on the day you fell—date, time, and where exactly you were?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Yes, yes—January eighth, twenty twenty-four, about six thirty in the morning. I was walking out to my car at Aspen Ridge Apartments in Aurora—it's managed by Greystar—and there was this slick patch of black ice, like glass. The lot hadn't been salted, hadn't been plowed, nothing, even though we'd had a pretty bad snowstorm the night before."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "That sounds painful and really frustrating. Had you noticed ice buildup there before, or had you complained to management about winter maintenance?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Oh, Brenda, I've complained so many times I'm embarrassed to say it again. I have emails to the property manager, Vanessa Thornton, from November and from December—I'm not talking one polite note, I'm talking follow-ups—because this same corner of the lot ices over every cold snap. I told them someone was going to get hurt."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "That's really helpful that you documented it. Do you still have those emails saved, and do you know roughly what you told her in them?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "I have them in my Gmail, screenshots too. I basically begged them to salt before sunrise because people leave for work in the dark—I'm a hairstylist, I open early—and I said the drainage is bad so it refreezes. Vanessa would say they'd 'put in a work order' and then… radio silence."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Were there any witnesses when you fell, or anyone who saw the condition of the lot right after?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Yes! Another resident, Miguel Ortiz—sweet man—was on his balcony with coffee and he saw the whole thing. He ran down and helped me sit up, and he took pictures of the ice with his phone, like close-ups, because he said, 'Carmen, they're going to act like this never happened.'"}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "That's excellent. How did you feel immediately after the fall, and what did you do for medical care?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "I went down hard on my tailbone and my right side—like, stars in my eyes. I was shaking, nauseous. I didn't even wait for an ambulance because I was scared I'd freeze out there; I drove myself to UCHealth Anschutz—I know, probably not smart, but the pain was unreal."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "I understand—you were trying to get help quickly. What did the doctors find?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Dr. Rajesh Gupta saw me in the ER. He told me I had a fractured coccyx and an L4-L5 herniated disc—MRI showed it bulging where it shouldn't be. I've been doing physical therapy at Colorado Spine & Sport, and I've had two epidural steroid injections already. The bills are stacking up—about twenty-eight thousand dollars so far."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Thank you for those specifics—that helps a lot. Do you have health insurance covering any of that?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "I have Cigna through the small business marketplace—because I own my own salon, Carmen's Salon & Spa, here in Aurora. So some of it's covered, some of it's copays and deductibles, but either way it's money flying out of my pocket while I'm barely working."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Tell me more about how this has affected your work. You mentioned you're on your feet all day—what's changed since January?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "It's devastating, honestly. I can't stand for long periods without my back locking up and my hip screaming. I've had to cancel clients—my regulars, people I've done for years—and I've hired a part-time replacement stylist just to keep the lights on. I'm estimating I'm down about twenty-eight hundred dollars a week, and we're at roughly ten weeks of that already."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "That is a huge hit for a small business. Have you kept any records of the canceled appointments or payroll for the part-time stylist?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Yes—my booking app shows the cancellations, and I have Venmo and payroll stubs for the part-time girl. I also have texts from clients saying they're going somewhere else because I can't guarantee times—breaks my heart, Brenda, I'm passionate about what I do; this isn't just money, it's my reputation."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "I hear you. Switching gears for a moment—do you know whether Aspen Ridge or Greystar carries liability insurance? Any letters or claim numbers yet?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "I don't know the carrier name off the top of my head—I'm assuming a place that big has insurance—but nobody from management has handed me a policy number. I didn't want to say the wrong thing to them, you know? I just want someone professional to deal with Greystar because I'm tired of being nice."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Completely fair. You mentioned another attorney—what happened there?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Ugh. I had a consultation, sent him my ER paperwork and the November and December emails to Vanessa, and then he went quiet—voicemail, email, nothing. I felt so small, like my case wasn't 'flashy' enough. So when a friend said Morgan & Associates actually calls people back, I wrote your number on a sticky note in big letters."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "I'm really glad you reached us, Carmen. What's the best phone number and email to reach you, and your mailing address if it's different from the apartment?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Phone is seven two zero, five five five, six one eight three. Email is carmen dot delgado dot salon at gmail dot com—all lowercase. I still live at Aspen Ridge for now, same unit on file with the leasing office—I'll spell anything you need."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Perfect. Just to recap: slip on untreated black ice on January eighth at Aspen Ridge under Greystar, documented complaints to Vanessa Thornton in November and December, witness Miguel Ortiz with photos, care at UCHealth Anschutz with Dr. Gupta, fractured coccyx and L4-L5 herniation, PT at Colorado Spine & Sport, two injections, roughly twenty-eight thousand in medical bills with Cigna, and major income loss for Carmen's Salon & Spa with a hired replacement—does that sound right?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Yes, that's everything—I'm a little rambling, I know, but it's all true. I'm worried my clients won't come back even after I heal, and I'm furious that I warned them in writing."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "You gave exactly the kind of detail we need. Next steps: I'm assigning this to our intake team to pull your records list, we'll send you a retainer packet and a medical authorization so we can order UCHealth and therapy notes, and we'll reach out about those emails and Miguel's photos. Expect a follow-up within one business day."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Okay, okay—that actually makes me breathe easier. Thank you, Brenda. I'll watch my email for the packet."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "You're welcome, Carmen. We're going to take this seriously. If anything new comes up—another bill, another message from Vanessa—just forward it to us. Take care of yourself today."}], "outcome_status": "settled", "outcome_value": 97500}
{"id": "3be963bb-fe17-4095-b251-95703038093b", "transcript": [{"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Thank you for calling. This is Diana. How can I help you today?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Hi, um—yeah. I'm Kevin Michael O'Brien. I'm not even totally sure I should be doing this. My dad's a retired insurance adjuster and he kept saying I should at least, like, document what happened. So I'm kind of just trying to understand what that even means."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "I appreciate you reaching out, Kevin. There's no pressure on this call—we can go at your pace. When you're ready, can you tell me, in your own words, what happened?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Okay. So it was November 25th, 2024—the day after Thanksgiving. I was at my best friend Brian Chen's house for a friendsgiving thing. Address was 1847 Cascade Avenue in Colorado Springs. Brian had just mopped the kitchen tiles after cooking, and I walked in and my foot went out from under me. I landed really hard on my lower back on the tile."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "I'm sorry that happened. Did you get medical care afterward?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Yeah, I went to Penrose Hospital urgent care the next day. Dr. Sarah Williams saw me. She said it was a deep bruise or contusion on my lower back and mild muscle strain. I've been doing stretches and taking over-the-counter stuff. I've missed four shifts at REI—I'm part-time there—and I'm also in the MBA program at UCCS part-time."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Thank you for those details. Roughly what are you looking at in medical expenses so far?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Maybe around eight hundred dollars total, between the copay and a follow-up. I have student health insurance through UCCS. Brian feels awful and he actually offered to just pay the bills himself. I don't—I really don't want this to turn into something where I'm going after my friend."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "That makes sense, and a lot of people feel that way when they're hurt at someone else's home. If there's a renter's insurance policy, the claim is typically made against the policy itself—not a lawsuit against Brian as a person. It's similar to how car insurance works after a fender bender."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Is it possible to do it that way? Like, I've heard Brian has renter's insurance through Lemonade. If it went through insurance, would Brian even have to know, or would it, I don't know, mess him up personally?"}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "I want to be straight with you: Brian would almost certainly need to be involved to open a claim, because the policy is his. And while it's not the same as suing him, a paid claim can sometimes affect premiums or renewal pricing—so he could see a rate impact. It's not always dramatic, but it's not something I'd promise won't happen."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Yeah, that's what I'm afraid of. We've been friends forever. I keep thinking, what if this makes things weird, or he thinks I'm choosing money over the friendship? I'm not trying to—I just don't know what I'm supposed to do."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "It sounds like you're trying to balance being fair to yourself with protecting a relationship you care about. That's valid. Some people choose to handle smaller bills out of pocket for exactly that reason; others use insurance specifically so the friendship isn't carrying a financial weight long term."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Right. And my dad keeps saying 'document, document,' like I'm going to wake up in more pain or something. I've never had anything like this before—no prior injuries, no legal stuff. I'm mostly calling to understand if there's a path that doesn't feel like I'm suing Brian."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "A renter's liability claim is usually administrative: notice to the insurer, bills and records, sometimes a short statement. It's not automatically a court case. That said, insurers investigate, and Brian may need to cooperate. It's not invisible."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Okay. Is it possible to start something and then stop if it gets uncomfortable? Or—sorry, I'm asking a lot of 'is it possible' questions. I'm just really tentative about all of this."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "You're asking good questions. Generally you can choose not to pursue a claim, but timing matters for evidence and deadlines, so it's worth knowing the policy's reporting window if you go the insurance route."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Got it. If you need my contact info for your notes or whatever—my phone is 719-555-2088 and my email is kobrien.uccs@gmail.com. Again, I'm not sure I'm signing up for anything. I'm just trying to figure out if there's a clean way to do this."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Thank you, Kevin. I've got Kevin Michael O'Brien, that number, and the email. For our office's purposes, is there anything else you want to add about how you're feeling physically now?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "It's improving, slowly. I'm still stiff some mornings. I guess I'm also wondering—if the bills are 'small,' does that mean nobody would help anyway? I don't want to waste anyone's time."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "You're not wasting time by asking. Based on what you've described—limited damages, strong friendship concerns, and a path that may hinge on Brian cooperating with a Lemonade claim—this is likely too small and factually complicated for our firm to take on as a representation. We typically handle matters where the economics and liability picture justify full litigation if needed."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Oh. Okay. I think I'm almost relieved? I mean, I didn't want to feel like I was being pushed into something against Brian. But I also don't know what I'm supposed to tell my dad."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "You can tell him you spoke with an intake team, got a clear picture of how renter's insurance fits in, and that the damages are modest enough that full attorney involvement isn't a fit here. You still documented the basics: date, location at 1847 Cascade, provider at Penrose and Dr. Williams, and your expenses."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "That actually helps. So your honest suggestion is what—just eat the cost, or talk to Brian?"}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "If you want to preserve the friendship and keep things transparent, a practical next step is to have a calm conversation with Brian about whether he's willing to file a liability claim on his renter's policy. You could offer to share the bills and chart notes so it's straightforward for him. If he's not comfortable, you'll at least know and can decide from there."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Yeah. That's awkward, but it feels more honest than doing something behind his back. Thank you for explaining all that—and for not making me feel like a bad friend for even calling."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "You're welcome, Kevin. If anything changes or you have new treatment, keep your records organized. I hope your back keeps improving."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Thanks, Diana. I'll—I'll figure it out. Bye."}], "outcome_status": "dropped", "outcome_value": 0}
{"id": "9e4c72df-90c3-4fae-bfd0-6d7ff75abf6f", "transcript": [{"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Thank you for calling Finch Intake, this is Alex. How are you holding up today?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Hi Alex—I'm Tamika. I'm… okay, I guess. Nervous, but I'm trying to stay practical. I was in a really bad rideshare crash last fall and I still feel like I'm living inside the sound of metal bending."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "I'm really sorry you're carrying that. Can you walk me through what happened, in your own words? Take your time."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "My full name is Tamika Renee Johnson—I'm thirty-one. I'm a fourth-grade teacher at Rosa Parks Elementary in Decatur. On October twelfth, twenty twenty-four, I was in a Lyft headed to Hartsfield-Jackson for a work conference. The driver was a man named Victor; I've got his info right in the Lyft app."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Got it. Where were you when the collision happened?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Memorial Drive and Candler Road in Decatur. Victor rolled through a stop sign—just rolled it—and this Honda Accord, driven by a woman named Shonda Williams, slammed into us. T-boned us on the passenger side. That's where I was sitting. My body remembers the sideways jerk before anything else."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "That sounds terrifying. Were emergency services involved?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "DeKalb County Fire had to extract me. Sirens, cutters, the whole scene. They got me out and took me to Emory University Hospital Midtown. I can still smell the ambulance vinyl when I think about it."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "What injuries were you diagnosed with, and who treated you?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Fractured left wrist—distal radius—plus whiplash and cervical strain. Dr. Anna Petrov, orthopedics, did surgery: plate and screws. I'm in a cast for six more weeks. And I've been diagnosed with PTSD by Dr. Lawrence Chen, a psychiatrist at Emory. Some days the anxiety sits on my chest like a weight."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Thank you for trusting me with that. How has this affected work and your day-to-day?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "I've been out about two months. The school brought in a long-term sub for my kids—my actual kids in my class, I mean—and I'm on short-term disability through DeKalb County Schools. I love my job; not being there feels like I've left the room mid-sentence."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Do you have documentation that helps us reconstruct the ride and the timeline?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Yes—my phone has the Lyft ride receipt with timestamps and the route. It shows I was an active passenger when this happened. I keep opening it like proof that I'm not imagining how fast everything changed."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "That's helpful evidence. Do you have the police report information?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "The report number is twenty-four-dash-D-K-dash-seven-three-eight-nine-one—24-DK-73891. I wrote it on a sticky note on my fridge so I wouldn't lose it."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Let's talk insurance, because rideshare cases have layers. Often the driver's personal auto policy excludes commercial or rideshare use, so people assume there's no coverage—but if you were in an active Lyft ride, Lyft typically carries a commercial liability policy, often up to a million dollars while the ride is in progress. We still investigate every policy, but that's the general framework."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "That's exactly what I was trying to understand. Victor's personal insurance might wash its hands of this because it was rideshare—but Lyft has that million-dollar liability policy for active rides, right? I don't want to guess wrong and leave money on the table."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "You're thinking about it the right way. We'll confirm the ride phase—matched, en route, in trip—and match that to the applicable coverage. What about your medical bills and health insurance?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Medical bills are around fifty-two thousand dollars so far. My health insurance is through my employer—United Healthcare. I'm getting EOBs that make my eyes cross, but I'm keeping everything."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Are you able to drive or commute comfortably right now?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "I… can't drive without panic climbing up my throat. So I've been taking Lyft and Uber to work—which is its own kind of irony, right? I get in the back seat and grip my bag like it's a life raft. I hate that something I used to do without thinking now feels like a gamble."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "That makes sense neurologically after trauma—your nervous system is trying to protect you. We'll want Dr. Chen's records and any treatment notes that document how this affects daily functioning, including transportation."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Okay. That helps to hear it said plainly. I don't want people to think I'm dramatic—I teach nine-year-olds all day; I'm not someone who falls apart for attention."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "You're not dramatic; you're injured. Have you spoken with any other attorneys yet?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "One. He wanted a forty percent contingency fee, and it just felt steep in my gut—like I'd be trading one anxiety for another. I need clarity and fairness, not a hard sell."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "I appreciate you saying that. Our fee structure is different—we can send you a written outline so you can compare apples to apples, and you can review it without pressure."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "I'd like that. If you need to reach me, my phone is 404-555-6847 and my email is tamika.johnson.teach@gmail.com."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Perfect, Tamika Renee Johnson—404-555-6847, tamika.johnson.teach@gmail.com. I'll repeat the key facts back: Lyft passenger, October 12, 2024, Memorial Drive and Candler Road, T-bone into passenger side, Emory Midtown, Dr. Petrov and Dr. Chen, police report 24-DK-73891, Lyft receipt on your phone, employer United Healthcare, STD through DeKalb County Schools."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Yes—that's all correct. Victor and Shonda's names are in my notes too, from the app and the report."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Here's what happens next: we'll calendar a deeper case review, request the police report and your medical records packages, and outline the rideshare coverage analysis for Lyft versus any personal policies. You'll get a clear written plan before anything moves forward."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Thank you, Alex. I feel a little less alone having it organized like that."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "You're welcome, Tamika. We'll follow up shortly with those next steps and the fee comparison sheet. Take care of that wrist—and be gentle with yourself on the rides. We're going to help you navigate this."}], "outcome_status": "settled", "outcome_value": 178000}
{"id": "b4067cef-f5a4-410c-acc5-f1fced84c3cc", "transcript": [{"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Thank you for calling Finch Intake, this is Carlos. How can I help you today?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Hi Carlos, this is Jennifer Nakamura-Smith. I'm calling about a trip-and-fall on a badly broken City of Denver sidewalk in Cheesman Park. I'd like to understand whether you handle municipal liability and what I need to do next—I've already pulled some of the statutes."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Absolutely, Jennifer. We handle premises and governmental cases. If you're ready, walk me through what happened in your own words, including where you were in the park."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "On January 10, 2025, around 7 a.m., I was jogging on the east side of Cheesman Park, near the Cheesman Park Pavilion. I hit a severely broken, upheaved concrete slab—I'd estimate it was raised about three inches from tree-root growth—and I went down hard."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "I'm sorry that happened. Were you alone, and did anyone assist you after the fall?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Another jogger stopped—his name is Tom Hadley. I couldn't put weight on my ankle, so he called 911 for me. EMS took me from the park to Denver Health Medical Center."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "What injuries were you diagnosed with, and who treated you in the ER or follow-up?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Dr. Amir Hussain diagnosed a grade 3 ankle sprain with torn ligaments—specifically my ATFL and CFL—plus deep abrasions. I was placed in a walking boot and given crutches."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "What does your recovery look like now—physical therapy, imaging, anything surgical on the table?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "I've been in physical therapy at Peak Physical Therapy twice a week for six weeks. The ankle still feels unstable, and Dr. Hussain has mentioned a possible Brostrom procedure if it doesn't stabilize."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Did you document the defect or the city's response after you reported it?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Yes—I photographed the sidewalk section on my phone before the ambulance arrived. I reported it to Denver Parks and Recreation; they eventually sent someone out and put orange cones around it three days later, and I photographed that too."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Tell me a bit about your work and day-to-day impact. I know you're a project manager—are you losing time or income?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "I'm 39, a project manager at Raytheon here in Denver—it's a desk job. I've mostly worked from home, so lost wages are minimal. The bigger hit is personal: I'm an avid runner and was training for the Colfax Marathon in May. Running is my stress relief and a big part of my identity, and I'm more frustrated about that than the acute pain."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Understood—that's a real quality-of-life loss. What are your medical bills so far, and how is coverage working?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "I'm at about $9,500 in medical bills so far. If I need surgery, I've seen estimates that could add $25,000 or more. My health insurance is Anthem through Raytheon."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Who do you understand to be the responsible party?"}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "The City of Denver, as the entity responsible for that sidewalk in the park. I also read that Colorado has a 182-day notice requirement for claims against government entities, and I want to be sure I'm not missing a step or a deadline."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "You're well prepared—that notice requirement is exactly the kind of trap that sinks otherwise strong cases. For governmental claims, we typically need to preserve the claim through the proper written notice process and calendar every statutory deadline aggressively."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Good. To keep this efficient: is that 182-day period usually counted as calendar days, and does the clock generally start from the date of injury or from when a reasonable person would have discovered the claim? I want the conservative interpretation."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "We treat these as calendar-day deadlines and assume the earliest reasonable trigger unless records show otherwise. Practically, that means we don't flirt with the window—we file compliant notice early and build the file in parallel with your treatment."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Perfect. My phone is 303-555-4871 and my email is jennifer.ns@outlook.com. Full legal name again is Jennifer Nakamura-Smith."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Got it—303-555-4871 and jennifer.ns@outlook.com for Jennifer Nakamura-Smith. Quick recap: dangerous, raised sidewalk near the Cheesman Park Pavilion; EMS transport; grade 3 sprain under Dr. Hussain with PT at Peak and possible Brostrom surgery; strong photo documentation including the city's delayed cone response; municipal defendant with an active notice deadline."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "That's accurate. I have no prior relevant injuries and no open legal issues—this would be my first claim."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Next steps on our side: we'll request your Denver Health records, PT notes, any imaging, and copies of your photos and Parks correspondence. We'll also prepare and file the governmental notice well inside the 182-day window so your rights are protected while we investigate liability and damages."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Please prioritize the notice piece—I don't want calendar math to be what costs me the marathon or the case."}, {"speaker": "Intake Specialist", "text": "Agreed. I'll email you an engagement packet within the hour with a checklist and a highlighted summary of the claims deadline so it's impossible to miss. If anything changes medically—especially if surgery is scheduled—tell us immediately."}, {"speaker": "Caller", "text": "Will do. Thanks, Carlos—this is exactly the level of urgency I was looking for."}], "outcome_status": "settled", "outcome_value": 62000}
